. /*H4. Having daughters leads to a larger increase in the support of gender eq
> uality for men than for women (with gender equality measured by attitudes). 
> That is, denoting X as a measure of support for gender equality, 
> (X for male respondents with daughters − X for male respondents without daugh
> ters) >  
> (X for female respondents with daughters − X for female respondents without d
> aughters) 
> */
