. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 * 
. 
.         * Please add a verbal description of your model here
. 
.         * We assume that a scale composing of various items in support for ge
> nder equality (attitude_scale_01) is a good measure of support for gender equ
> ality.
.         * if having a daughter, a larger increase in the support of gender eq
> uality will be observed for men than for women (the interaction between being
>  a women and having a daughter will be negative (assuming that the main effec
> t of having a daughter is positive).
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with attitude_
> scale_01 as dependent variable and the dummy variable d_daughter as independe
> nt variable, and the dummy variable d_sex as the interaction variable.
. 
. 
. //Interactions
. regress attitude_scale_01 i.d_daughter##i.d_sex, cluster(hid) coeflegend //ge
> tting coeflabels 

