. *Having a daughter (main effect) should be (+) associated with stronger suppo
> rt for gender equality
. *women#daughters should be (-): for men the gender equality effect should str
> onger when they have daughters (compared to sons) and compared to women. 
. 
. 
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS * 
. 
.         * Extract the required statistics
. 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient1 = _b[1.d_daughter]

.                 local coefficient2 = _b[1.d_sex]

.                 local coefficient = _b[1.d_daughter#1.d_sex]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[1.d_daughter#1.d_sex]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "t"

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value
.                 local p_value = _b[1.d_daughter#1.d_sex] / _se[1.d_daughter#1
> .d_sex]

.                 local p_value = 2 * ttail(e(df_r), abs(`p_value'))

. 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
.                 local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.                 * (vii) number of participants
.                 quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

.                 local num_participants : word count `participants'

. 
.                 * (viii) interpretation based of directionality and p-value
.                 local interpretation "negative coefficient is in line with hy
> pothesis"

.                 
.                 
